::heading level=1 id=compact-proof
Compaction Proof
::end

::paragraph id=compact-proof-method
For each sample, `reduction_bytes = md_bytes - packed_bytes` and `reduction_pct = reduction_bytes / md_bytes * 100`.
::end

::code id=compact-proof-metrics hidden lang=json
[
	{"sample":"A","md_bytes":1200,"packed_bytes":630,"reduction_bytes":570,"reduction_pct":47.50},
	{"sample":"B","md_bytes":980,"packed_bytes":520,"reduction_bytes":460,"reduction_pct":46.94},
	{"sample":"C","md_bytes":1440,"packed_bytes":760,"reduction_bytes":680,"reduction_pct":47.22}
]
::end

::html id=compact-proof-table
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Sample</th><th>Markdown (B)</th><th>Packed (B)</th><th>Reduction (B)</th><th>Reduction</th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td>A</td><td>1200</td><td>630</td><td>570</td><td>47.50%</td></tr>
		<tr><td>B</td><td>980</td><td>520</td><td>460</td><td>46.94%</td></tr>
		<tr><td>C</td><td>1440</td><td>760</td><td>680</td><td>47.22%</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
::end

::svg id=compact-proof-plot
<svg viewBox="0 0 720 150" role="img" aria-label="Reduction per sample against a full-width 100 percent: A 47.50, B 46.94, C 47.22">
	<g font-family="monospace" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">
		<text x="0" y="16" fill-opacity="0.55">reduction (%) — the outline is 100%</text>
		<text x="0" y="52">A</text>
		<text x="0" y="88">B</text>
		<text x="0" y="124">C</text>
	</g>
	<g fill="currentColor" fill-opacity="0.28">
		<rect x="40" y="40" width="285" height="16"/>
		<rect x="40" y="76" width="282" height="16"/>
		<rect x="40" y="112" width="283" height="16"/>
	</g>
	<g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-opacity="0.25">
		<rect x="40" y="40" width="600" height="16"/>
		<rect x="40" y="76" width="600" height="16"/>
		<rect x="40" y="112" width="600" height="16"/>
	</g>
	<g font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity="0.55">
		<text x="652" y="52">47.50</text>
		<text x="652" y="88">46.94</text>
		<text x="652" y="124">47.22</text>
	</g>
</svg>
::end

::paragraph id=compact-proof-outcome
All three samples land within six-tenths of a point of each other, so the saving is a property of the encoding rather than of any one payload.
::end
